# --- credentials: never commit, the repo is public --------------------------
# The KDB-X license key (kc.lic / k4.lic) lives in ~/.kx and is delivered by an
# authenticated installer. It has no business here, but a stray `cp` while
# debugging is exactly how these get committed. Cheap insurance.
*.lic
.env
.env.*
*.pem
*.key
secrets.*

# --- macOS / editors ---------------------------------------------------------
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
*.swp
*~
.vscode/
.idea/

# --- Claude Code local state -------------------------------------------------
# .claude/skills/ IS tracked on purpose; only local machine state is ignored.
.claude/settings.local.json

# --- eval / verify scratch ---------------------------------------------------
# Goldens (*.expected) and reference solutions (*.ref.q) ARE tracked, and so are
# the eval's saved model outputs under eval/runs/ — an article claiming a result
# ships the raw material behind it (see eval/PLAN-M2.md §3). What is ignored is
# the transient scoring scratch: eval/README.md's correctness snippet writes
# cand.q / cand.out / cand.err into the working directory, 30 times over.
*.actual
cand.q
cand.out
cand.err
eval/.work/

# --- python helpers ----------------------------------------------------------
__pycache__/
*.pyc

# --- guard, not a workflow ---------------------------------------------------
# There is no drafts/ (CLAUDE.md rule 3): an unfinished lesson stays on its
# feature branch until `make verify` is green, so nothing half-verified ever
# reaches the public default branch. This entry exists only so that if someone
# creates one anyway, it cannot be committed by accident.
drafts/
